{"id":"0b3c8928cef7eaa4","group":"89","path":"89/89-df-gl-normal-form.md","title":"GL Normal Form","display":"df-gl-normal-form — GL Normal Form","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-df-gl-normal-form","aliases":["89-df-gl-normal-form"],"display":"df-gl-normal-form — GL Normal Form","depends_on":["[[89-df-modal-formula]]","[[89-df-modal-sequent]]","[[89-df-box-modality]]","[[89-df-modal-negation]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-df-gl-normal-form"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-df-gl-normal-form</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-gl-normal-form — GL Normal Form"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"56c1b5b75a32ca1d\" href=\"?note=56c1b5b75a32ca1d\" title=\"89-df-modal-formula\">89-df-modal-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca21b68a25f1afc2\" href=\"?note=ca21b68a25f1afc2\" title=\"89-df-modal-sequent\">89-df-modal-sequent</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d246470e97fec132\" href=\"?note=d246470e97fec132\" title=\"89-df-box-modality\">89-df-box-modality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5dbb49ee42ea9770\" href=\"?note=5dbb49ee42ea9770\" title=\"89-df-modal-negation\">89-df-modal-negation</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prop}\">\\(\\mathrm{Prop}\\)</span> is the set of propositional variables.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigwedge\">\\(\\bigwedge\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigvee\">\\(\\bigvee\\)</span> are the recursively defined finite-sequence\nfolds from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ca21b68a25f1afc2\" href=\"?note=ca21b68a25f1afc2\" title=\"89-df-modal-sequent\">89-df-modal-sequent</a>, including their empty cases.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gl\\text{-}normal\\text{-}form}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal{L}_{\\Box}\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\mathrm{Prop}\n\\cup\\{\\neg p\\mid p\\in\\mathrm{Prop}\\}\n\\cup\\{\\Box B,\\neg\\Box B\\mid B\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{NF}_{\\mathrm{GL}}\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\bigvee\\langle\\bigwedge\\Gamma_i\\mid i&lt;m\\rangle\n\\ \\middle|\\\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\forall i&lt;m\\;(\\Gamma_i\\in\\mathcal L_{\\Box}^{&lt;\\omega})\n\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gl\\text{-}normal\\text{-}form}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal{L}_{\\Box}\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\mathrm{Prop}\n\\cup\\{\\neg p\\mid p\\in\\mathrm{Prop}\\}\n\\cup\\{\\Box B,\\neg\\Box B\\mid B\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{NF}_{\\mathrm{GL}}\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\bigvee\\langle\\bigwedge\\Gamma_i\\mid i&lt;m\\rangle\n\\ \\middle|\\\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\forall i&lt;m\\;(\\Gamma_i\\in\\mathcal L_{\\Box}^{&lt;\\omega})\n\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>GL 正规形把每个最外层盒公式视为一个命题原子，并取有限析取范式。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m=0\">\\(m=0\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma_i=\\langle\\rangle\">\\(\\Gamma_i=\\langle\\rangle\\)</span> 的边界分别由\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigvee\\langle\\rangle=\\bot\">\\(\\bigvee\\langle\\rangle=\\bot\\)</span> 和 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigwedge\\langle\\rangle=\\top\">\\(\\bigwedge\\langle\\rangle=\\top\\)</span> 覆盖。</li>\n<li>GL正常形式简化证明分析</li>\n<li>GL正常形式是完全性证明的工具</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-modal-formula","status":"resolved","id":"56c1b5b75a32ca1d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-modal-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-modal-sequent","status":"resolved","id":"ca21b68a25f1afc2","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-modal-sequent]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-box-modality","status":"resolved","id":"d246470e97fec132","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-box-modality]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-modal-negation","status":"resolved","id":"5dbb49ee42ea9770","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-modal-negation]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-modal-sequent","status":"resolved","id":"ca21b68a25f1afc2","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\bigwedge$ and $\\bigvee$ are the recursively defined finite-sequence\nfolds from [[89-df-modal-sequent]], including their empty cases.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prop}","display":false},{"tex":"\\bigwedge","display":false},{"tex":"\\bigvee","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gl\\text{-}normal\\text{-}form}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal{L}_{\\Box}\n&\\coloneqq\n\\mathrm{Prop}\n\\cup\\{\\neg p\\mid p\\in\\mathrm{Prop}\\}\n\\cup\\{\\Box B,\\neg\\Box B\\mid B\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{NF}_{\\mathrm{GL}}\n&\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\bigvee\\langle\\bigwedge\\Gamma_i\\mid i<m\\rangle\n\\ \\middle|\\\nm\\in\\omega\\land\n\\forall i<m\\;(\\Gamma_i\\in\\mathcal L_{\\Box}^{<\\omega})\n\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"m=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\Gamma_i=\\langl